sentences.t:
Nós çercamos el escaño por curiar nuestro señor,
fasta do despertó mio Çid, el que Valençia gañó;
levantós del escaño e f[o]s poral león;

sentences.l:
We surrounded the bench to guard our lord,
until when awoke my Çid, he who Valençia won;
he-rose-himself from-the bench and went-himself toward-the lion;

sentences.t:
Quando se tornó el buen Campeador,
a sos vassallos, víolos aderredor;
demandó por s[o]s yernos, ninguno non falló!

sentences.l:
When himself turned the good Campeador,
his vassals, he-saw-them around;
he-asked for his sons-in-law, none not he-found!

I-challenge-you the body for wicked and for traitor.
This-to-you I-will-fight here before king don Alfons
for daughters of-the Çid, don Elvira and doña Sol:

sentences.t:
por quanto las dexastes menos valedes vos;
ellas son mugieres e vos sodes varones,
en todas guisas más valen que vos.

sentences.l:
because them you-left worth-less are you;
they are women and you are men,
in all ways more they-are-worth than you.

sentences.t:
Quando f[o]re la lid, si ploguiere al Criador,
tú lo otorgarás a guisa de traydor;
de quanto he dicho verdadero seré yo.”

sentences.l:
When shall-be the fight, if it-shall-please to-the Creator,
you it will-confess in manner of traitor;
of as-much-as I-have said truthful shall-be I.”

sentences.t:
Porque dexamos sus fijas aun no nos repentimos;
mientra que bivan pueden aver sospiros:
lo que les fiziemos se[e]r les ha retraydo.

sentences.l:
Because we-left his daughters still not ourselves we-repent;
while that they-live they-can have sighs:
what to-them we-did to-be to-them it-has cast-up.

sentences.t:
Lo del león no se te deve olbidar;
saliste por la puerta, metistet al corral,
fústed meter tras la viga lagar;

sentences.l:
The-business of-the lion not itself to-you ought to-forget;
you-went-out by the door, you-put-yourself into-the yard,
you-went-yourself to-put behind the beam press;

sentences.t:
A[n]su[o]r Gonçal[v]ez entrava por el palaçio.
manto armiño e un brial rastrando;
vermejo viene, ca era almorzado.

sentences.l:
A[n]su[o]r Gonçal[v]ez was-entering through the palace.
mantle ermine and a tunic trailing;
red he-comes, for he-was breakfasted.

sentences.t:
al uno dizen Ojarra e al otro Yéñego Simen[ones],
el uno es [del] infante de Navarra [rogador],
e el otro [es] [del] ifante de Aragón;

sentences.l:
to-the one they-call Ojarra and to-the other Yéñego Simen[ones],
the one is [of-the] Infante of Navarra [petitioner],
and the other [is] [of-the] Infante of Aragón;
